# `luria index` writes views next to the sources when an example is run in
# place. None of it is committed: `tests/test_examples.py` builds each example
# in a temporary directory and generates there, so nothing here can become a
# stale committed view — which is the failure these examples exist to argue
# against.
*/docs/*
!*/docs/README.md
# The one hand-written page that is not an index: the source document
# `constitution/` decomposes. It lives under `docs/` so the reference
# machinery scans it — a claim in it that names a document in the record has
# to be a resolvable link like any other prose.
!*/docs/constitution.md
*/decisions/README.md
*/decisions/tags/
